  <page_number>47</page_number>
  <running_head>De Duellis</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quæ</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">&amp; quasi præsentem adversa-</l>
    <l n="2">rium, sic palum omni impe-</l>
    <l n="3">tu, omnique bellandi arte ten-</l>
    <l n="4">taret. Quod exercitium tantò</l>
    <l n="5">gratius erat, quantò magis ex-</l>
    <l n="6">tra discriminis aut periculi ul-</l>
    <l n="7">lius aleam certator in hoc con-</l>
    <l n="8">stitueretur. Quo cum fermè</l>
    <l n="9">convenit hodiernus exercendi</l>
    <l n="10">equites modus. Quando sin-</l>
    <l n="11">guli utrinque è turmâ in se</l>
    <l n="12">mutuò iruunt, experimentum</l>
    <l n="13">daturi uter altero tractandis</l>
    <l n="14">armis magis idoneus, in exo-</l>
    <l n="15">nerandis sclopis minoribus,</l>
    <l n="16">quibus invicem petunt, cele-</l>
    <l n="17">rior, iisque explosis, ad gla-</l>
    <l n="18">dium stringendum sit expedi-</l>
    <l n="19">tior. Idem quod in peditibus</l>
    <l n="20">observatur, qui vel soli, vel</l>
    <l n="21">singuli in singulos missi, exer-</l>
    <l n="22">centur, quo tractandis sclopis</l>
    <l n="23">reddantur aptiores.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Verùm prætereunda non</l>
    <l n="25">videtur ars laniftica, quam</l>
    <l n="26">Itali <i>Scrimiam</i> appellant.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed hyphens at line ends kept as printed. No marginal notes, no footnotes. The word "palum" and the accent on "Verùm" are as they appear in the scan; no other doubtful readings.</notes>
